WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.050 --> 00:00:01.913
Revocation has its own timing.

2
00:00:01.913 --> 00:00:05.141
Entra checks the issuing
authority's revocation list,

3
00:00:05.141 --> 00:00:08.799
but it caches that list and
doesn't support live status checks,

4
00:00:08.799 --> 00:00:13.175
so a revoked card stops working on the
authority's schedule, not instantly.

5
00:00:13.175 --> 00:00:17.712
That's why the account block and token
revocation matter: they close Entra now.

6
00:00:17.712 --> 00:00:19.412
Devices are the other trap.

7
00:00:19.412 --> 00:00:23.809
Intune revokes a device certificate
when you retire or wipe the device,

8
00:00:23.809 --> 00:00:26.938
but not when you delete the
user or pull the license.

9
00:00:26.938 --> 00:00:31.296
So the order is retire first and
delete last, and remove certificate

10
00:00:31.296 --> 00:00:35.888
assignments before revoking by hand,
or the device simply gets a new one.

11
00:00:35.888 --> 00:00:38.380
That order becomes the leaver sequence.
